# Finance lazy workspace bindings (P4-D3)

API and admin-web finance codegen must not **statically** import every `@app-tour/workspace-*` host/finance module at process load. Static fan-in pulls product adapters into the cold graph even when no tenant uses that workspace.

## Problem

| Generated file | Pre-lazy shape | Cost |
| -------------- | -------------- | ---- |
| `workspace-finance-chart-of-accounts-bindings.generated.ts` | `import { LEDGER_ACCOUNTS } from "@app-tour/workspace-denali/host/finance"` × N | Eager CoA constants |
| `workspace-finance-dependency-bindings.generated.ts` | Static adapter class imports + `() => new Adapter()` | Eager ledger/receipt factories |
| `workspace-finance-event-reaction-bindings.generated.ts` | Static reaction class imports + `create(hostIo?)` | Eager TourCreated reaction graph |
| `workspace-finance-obligation-bindings.generated.ts` | Static `resolveDenaliRegistrationObligationMinor` import | Eager pricing bind |
| `workspace-finance-ops-bindings.generated.ts` (web) | Static `DEFAULT_FINANCE_OPS_MANIFEST` + theme resolvers | Eager admin ops panels |
| `workspace-finance-bindings.generated.ts` / `…-capabilities.generated.ts` | `import { DENALI_WORKSPACE_TYPE } from "@app-tour/workspace-denali"` | Eager package root for string constants |

At N workspaces this is O(N) product packages on every API / finance-hub boot path that touches any finance generated module.

## Decision

Emitters in `scripts/codegen/workspace-registry/domains/finance.mjs` produce **data + async loaders** only — no top-level `import` from product packages.

```text
resolve(workspaceType | pluginId)
  → lookup binding (sync, fail-closed / soft-null)
  → await import(specifier)   // Node / bundler module cache after first hit
  → construct / return export
```

| Slice | Status | Loader shape | Runtime API |
| ----- | ------ | ------------ | ----------- |
| **P4-D3.a** CoA | DONE | `loadAccounts: async () => (await import(spec)).EXPORT` | `resolveFinanceChartOfAccounts` → **async** |
| **P4-D3.b** deps | DONE | `createLedgerPolicy` / `createReceiptDefaults` async factories | `resolveFinanceLedgerPolicy` / `ReceiptDefaults` / `resolveFinanceWorkspaceDependencies` → **async** |
| **P4-D3.b** event reaction | DONE | `create: async (hostIo?) => new (await import(spec)).Export(...)` | `resolveWorkspaceFinanceEventReaction` → **async** |
| **P4-D3.b** obligation | DONE | `loadResolve: async () => (await import(spec)).EXPORT` | `createFinanceObligationPort` → **async** |
| **P4-D3.c** web ops | DONE | `loadManifest: async (theme?) => …` | `resolveWorkspaceFinanceOpsManifest` / `resolveFinanceOpsCapabilityForHub` → **async** |
| **P4-D3.d** bindings / capabilities | DONE | JSON string literals from `workspaceTypes` (no product package import) | `isFinanceSupportedWorkspace` / `getFinanceWorkspaceCapabilities` stay **sync** |

```mermaid
sequenceDiagram
  participant Host as HTTP / outbox / recon / finance hub
  participant Reg as finance-* registry / ops panels
  participant Gen as *.generated.ts
  participant WS as workspace-*/host/finance

  Host->>Reg: await resolve*(id)
  Reg->>Gen: binding lookup (sync)
  alt unregistered
    Reg-->>Host: throw FINANCE_*_UNSUPPORTED / null (ops soft)
  else registered
    Gen->>WS: await import(specifier)
    WS-->>Gen: module exports
    Gen-->>Reg: port / manifest
    Reg-->>Host: ready
  end
```

## Composition root (API)

`getOrCreateFinanceServiceForWorkspaceType` is **async** and awaits dependency resolve before `createFinanceService`. Concurrent first-hit for the same `workspaceType` shares one in-flight promise so two HTTP requests cannot compose duplicate services.

`resolveFinanceServiceForTenant` / `resolveLazyFinanceService` already returned `Promise<FinanceService>` — they now correctly await the async getOrCreate path.

## Admin web (ops)

`FinanceCommandCenter` and `FinanceInstallmentsPanel` resolve ops capability in `useEffect` (async), not `useMemo`. Soft-null for unbound `pluginId` is unchanged — loading and unbound both render nothing until a capability arrives.

## Invariants

1. **Fail-closed (API)** — empty / unknown `workspaceType` still throws before import (same error codes).
2. **Soft-null (web ops)** — unbound `pluginId` → `null` (no Denali fallback).
3. **No computed dynamic import** — string literals only (`import("@app-tour/workspace-…")`) for import-boundary / depcruise.
4. **Platform booking projection** remains host-owned (`createBookingPaymentPort`) — not workspace-declared.
5. **`requiresHostIo`** stays a sync discriminant on event-reaction bindings; only `create` is async.
6. **`hasFinanceOpsManifest(pluginId)`** stays sync (id set only — no product import).
7. **Bindings / capabilities** use literal `workspaceType` strings from the manifest — importing `DENALI_WORKSPACE_TYPE` (or peers) is forbidden in those generated files.

## Regenerate / verify

```bash
pnpm run generate:workspace-registry
# API:
pnpm --filter @apps/api exec node --import tsx --test \
  src/workspace-finance/finance-dependency-registry.spec.ts \
  src/workspace-finance/finance-capability-certification.spec.ts \
  src/workspace-finance/finance-outbox-ownership.spec.ts \
  test/finance-obligation-denali.spec.ts
# Web:
pnpm --filter @apps/web exec node --import tsx --test test/finance-page.spec.ts
```

## CI regression (P4-D2)

Finance generated files are on the cold-path allowlist for `pnpm run guard:p4-cold-path-fan-in` (static product imports must stay **0**). See [`p4-d2-cold-path-fan-in-ci.mdoc`](./p4-d2-cold-path-fan-in-ci.mdoc).

